The Vietnamese press agency Xinhua reported that during a visit to Brunei Darussalam on the morning of February 11, Prime Minister Fan Ming-ying and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD).
The University of Brunei is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third in the region's university rankings.
The University of Brunei is one of the symbols of Vietnamese-Brunei cooperation in education and training.
Brunei University formally established a partnership with FPT University of Vietnam in July 2013, with the main area of cooperation being English language training.
In addition to foreign languages such as English, French, German, Japanese and Korean, Brunei University also incorporates Vietnamese into its curriculum.
During his visit to Universiti Brunei Darussalam, Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Thanh and his wife had an exchange with students of Vietnamese language classes.
Vice Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is pleased that more foreigners are learning Vietnamese and contributing positively to promoting the country’s cultural characteristics and local customs around the world.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng expressed his belief and hope that the Vietnamese language teaching staff at the University of Brunei will become increasingly strong; students in the Vietnamese class are becoming more interested in Vietnamese, working hard to learn it well, so they can use fluent Vietnamese soon and be ambassadors for friendly relations between the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also took the opportunity to communicate with Vietnamese students studying English at FPT-UBD Global Center in Chanh Muong District, Quang Nam Province, via video, to learn about their learning situation, especially during the pandemic.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diem said the cooperation between FPT University of Vietnam and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Centre, is a living symbol of the educational cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
At the same time, we hope that the students of the center will make greater progress in their studies and make positive contributions to the friendly and cooperative relations between Vietnam and the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly appreciated the achievements of the two countries in education cooperation during his discussions with the Minister of Education of Brunei and leaders of Brunei University. These achievements include the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese language in the teaching curriculum.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diệm hopes that Brunei University will continue to focus on ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the size of Vietnamese language classes.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, also highly evaluated the positive effects of cooperation between the two countries on the basis of the Memorandum of Understanding on Educational Cooperation signed in April 2014; he suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively carry out various short-term exchange training projects, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Premier Feng Mingzheng highly commends Brunei University’s establishment of its first branch in Vietnam; he believes that the university will continue to grow in both region and world; it is further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
During this opportunity, Premier Feng Mingzheng and his wife planted memorial trees on the campus of the University of Brunei Darussalam, and left messages on the memorial book.
Premier Feng Mingzheng wishes for the University of Brunei to continue its forward progress and contribute more powerfully to the education sector in Brunei; he also plans to deepen and broaden cooperation with Vietnam’s various educational training institutions.
(Finish)
