Many data decline, Taiwan's economy starts the year poorly - www.chinanews.com
Shanghai-based Xinhua News Agency reported that exports reached “five black” in January, with the manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) falling for seven consecutive months and consumer prices rising to the “three digits.” Taiwan’s authorities have recently released economic data for January 2023.
Experts say that Taiwan’s economy is underperforming in the new year and growth pressures are mounting.
According to the Taiwan authorities’ department in charge of financial affairs, the region’s exports amounted to US$31.51 billion in January this year, a year-on-year decrease of 21.2%, and the fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The exports of 11 major export categories declined in comparison to the same period last year.
Plastic rubber and its products, as well as optical instruments, had the sharpest declines of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Electronic component exports fell 20.1% year-on-year, marking the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, integrated circuits fell 18.3%, marking their largest decline in nearly a decade.
According to the department's statistics director, Ms. Kimena, this shows that the effects of weak demand in the consumer electronics industry are spreading and the electronics industry is entering a correction period.
Statistics show that in January, both imports and exports of Taiwan region fell, and the excess amount of exports was only 2.34 billion US dollars, which is the lowest level in the past three years.
The Financial Supervisory Service of the Taiwan authorities believes that the global terminal demand is reduced, and the adjustment of industrial inventory has inhibited the willingness of manufacturers to purchase raw materials. The export slump is unlikely to improve in the short term. The export decline of Taiwan in the first quarter of this year is expected to be worse than expected.
According to the Taiwan China Economic Research Institute, the seasonally adjusted Taiwan Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) in January was 40.4%, a decrease of 3.3 percentage points from December last year, and contracted for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring indicator system, the PMI is 50% as the demarcation line of prosperity and decline, and the index is greater than 50%, which represents prosperity expansion, and vice versa for contraction.
The January Taiwan PMI's five indicators include new orders, production and labor contraction, lower supplier delivery times, and shrinking inventories.
The six largest industries reported total PMI contraction, with each industry ranked according to the contraction rate as the electrical and mechanical equipment industry ((35.1%); electron fluorescent optics industry ((35.2%); chemical and biomedical engineering industry ((39.2%); basic raw materials industry ((42.4%); transportation industry ((42.6%) and food textile industry ((45.7%)).
In terms of prices, the “Directorate-General of Budget, Accounting and Statistics” of the Taiwan authorities announced that the CPI of Taiwan in January this year was 3.04%, which exceeded 3% for the first time since July last year.
Among them, the price of vegetables soared by 28.25%, creating a new high in 17 months.
Cao Zhijian, a special commissioner of the General Administration of Taizhou, said that the increase in the price of vegetables was indeed higher than expected, excluding the Spring Festival factor, and that the average CPI in January and February should be close to 2.71 percent in December last year, and that inflation pressures remained high.
Looking forward to this year's Taiwan economy, experts expressed pessimism after comprehensive reports by local media such as United Daily News and Yahoo Finance.
Liu Daing, professor of the Department of Economics at Taipei Central University, said that the export recession could cause problems in the cash flow of export manufacturers and increase the risk of default.
At the same time, declining orders have forced manufacturers to cut labor costs, which in turn affects the labor market and household incomes, thereby undermining consumer spending power.
Chu Daosheng of the Institute for Taiwan Economic Research believes that inflation in Europe and America is not yet under control, with demand continuing to decline, and expects Taiwan’s exports to continue to contract until the second half of this year.
Taiwan’s economy is export-driven; its growth will be weaker than last year because of sluggish exports.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthen restrictions on technology exports to China
The Wall Street Journal reported today that the United States is preparing to further tighten its technology exports to China after the balloon incident.
Current and former security officials say the balloon incident underscores the national security threat posed by China and will help generate more political support for beefing up U.S. technology protections.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martyn Rasser, a former senior CIA official who now works at the Washington think tank's Center for a New American Security.
"This is undoubtedly adding fuel to the fire and supports the hard-line view against China."
White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre said on Thursday that “we will also consider taking more extensive action to expose and respond to China’s larger-scale surveillance activities, which pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners.
The U.S. officials said they had notified the governments of more than 30 countries about the balloon incident and that international coordination was vital to counter the Chinese threat.
According to Emily Benso, a senior research fellow at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, in addition to the actions of the Biden administration, the newly established Select Committee on Strategic Competition between the United States and the Chinese Communist Party in the US House of Representatives may also put pressure on the United States to take more stringent measures to slow down China’s development.
She said that lawmakers would feel increasing pressure to take a tougher stance, which could push the White House to adopt a more aggressive policy.
Many who advocate tighter export controls are also pushing for the scope of regulation to be expanded to include industries like artificial intelligence, the Wall Street Journal reported.
The US government is also developing a foreign investment review program to examine whether US investments abroad pose a potential national security threat from China.
Analysts say the White House may face calls for a faster launch of the plan.
First batch of personal pension products launched for sale, with the shortest holding period of only 360 days - chinanews.com
Personal pension wealth management products were launched for the first time.
The 7 products offered by the home institution can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
The personal pension wealth product has finally been launched.
On February 10, China Wealth Management Network released the first list of personal pension wealth management products, and 7 personal pension wealth management products of Guotai Asset Management, Rural Commercial Bank Asset Management and China Postal Savings Fund Management were officially launched.
At this point, the "shelves" of the personal pension account are finally full of four types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and publicly offered mutual funds.
It is reported that all of the first batch of individual pension products are open-ended net-value type public offerings, with 5 new issues and 2 existing ones; except for one product which is a mixed-type, the remaining six products are fixed-income types.
The Beijing Youth Daily reporters found that 4 out of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed income products, and the shortest holding period was 365 days, 540 days, 720 days, and 1080 days, respectively, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, and 5.25% - 5.75%.
The remaining new product is "Postal Savings Wealth Add Yi Heng Hongjing Shortest Holding Period 1095 Days 1 ", which is also a fixed income product. It started collecting on February 10 and ended on February 19. The risk level is level 2.
One of the two existing products is Agricultural Bank of China Wealth Management “Agricultural Bank of China Unity·Spiritual” 360-day Science and Technology Innovation RMB Wealth Management Product, which is a mixed type investment product with a risk level of three.
Another product that is still available is "Postal Savings Wealth Additional Yinhe Hongjin Minimum Holding Period 365 Days No. 1," a fixed income product. It started collecting funds on December 30 last year and officially started operating on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net value on February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the opinion of the State Council Office on Promoting the Development of Individual Pensions, the financial products in which the funds of the Individual Pension Fund Account can be invested include banking, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public funds, etc.
The first personal pension wealth management product was sold, marking that personal pension investors can officially purchase wealth management products through the personal pension fund account.
The China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission formulated the Interim Measures for the Management of Personal Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies in November last year.
The Regulations provide that participants can purchase personal pension savings, personal pension wealth management products, personal pension insurance products, and personal pension open-end fund products through their individual pension funds accounts.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Administration of Taxation issued a notice, which clearly stated that the individual pension system would be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, and Hebei Shijiazhuang, as well as the Xiong’an New Area, and Jinci City, Shanxi.
As of December 31, 2022, there were 19.5 million participants in personal pension plans, with 6.13 million individuals contributing to them and total contributions amounting to RMB 1.42 billion.
Previously, the banks involved in the pilot only offered three categories of products: personal pension savings, personal pension insurance products and personal pension fund.
Now that a variety of personal pension wealth management products have gathered together, how should investors choose?
Experts from the Jilin Bank Product Development Department said that compared with other personal pension products, both pilot-stage pension-linked wealth management products and individual pension-linked wealth management products have three characteristics.
The first is stability, better risk management mechanisms, more robust investment strategies and concepts, and the implementation of independent third-party custody outside the parent bank.
II. Long-term nature, with most pilot phase pension products having maturities of five years or more; in the next issuance of individual pension products, the minimum holding period is generally one year, and encouraging a holding period of three years or more.
Third, it is inclusive. The threshold for purchasing products is low, and the starting point is generally 1 yuan, and some are as low as 0.01 yuan. The fees such as custody fees and management fees are more favorable.
Experts point out that investors should make their choices based on the product's characteristics and their own risk tolerance.
Individual pension savings have characteristics of long-term duration, high interest rates, and high safety, making them suitable for individuals with low risk tolerance; individual pension insurance products focus on protection, making them more appropriate for those who cannot bear investment risks but can accept stable returns; while individual pension product and open-end fund products do not guarantee returns or yields, they carry some investment risks, yet offer higher expected returns, which are more suitable for individuals with certain financial knowledge and higher risk tolerance.
Article/Reporter: Cheng Jie; Coordination: Chai Hua Bo
Newly Appointed Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Provincial and Ministerial Level Main Leaders Complete Study Course on Learning and Implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress Spirit - Rolling News - Huasheng Online - Hunan Daily
The seminar for new members, alternate members and provincial and ministerial leading cadres of the Central Committee on studying and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the 20th CPC National Congress was concluded.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large | medium | small】
Xinhua News Agency Beijing February 10th Message - The seminar for the newly elected members, alternate members and leading cadres of the provincial and ministerial level on learning and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the 20th CPC National Congress was concluded in the Central Party School (National Administrative College) on the afternoon of the 10th. Cai Qi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Secretary of the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection, attended the conclusion ceremony and made a summary speech.
He said that we should deeply study and implement the important spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's speech at the opening ceremony of the seminar, more firmly embrace the "two establishments", resolutely do the "two safeguards", enhance our capabilities, and work hard to push forward all aspects of Chinese-style modernization, and create a performance that can stand the test of history, practice and people in the process of building a socialist modernized country in all respects and promoting the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar period, all participants studied and deeply discussed with practical examples the important speeches of President Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar as well as the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC). This has deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues related to China’s modernization in its own way, enhanced their confidence and determination to advance China’s modernization under the leadership of the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi Jinping, strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission for fulfilling duties and responsibilities, and ensuring a good start in the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives of the seminar made speeches to report and share their learning achievements.
Cai Qi said that learning and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress is both the primary political task of the present and the future, and a long-term strategic task. It is necessary to promote learning and implementation in-depth, thorough and sincere, in accordance with the requirements of "comprehensive learning, comprehensive understanding, and comprehensive implementation".
To understand more profoundly the decisive significance of the “two establishments”, to firmly safeguard the core position of General Secretary Xi Jinping, to safeguard the authority of the Party Central Committee and the centralized and unified leadership, to continuously improve political judgment, political understanding and political execution, and to always maintain high consistency with the Party Central Committee with Xi Jinping as the core in thoughts, politics and actions.
We should strive to master the basic skills of Marxist theory, consciously use the innovative theory of the Party to arm our minds, guide our practice and promote our work, and work hard in deep study, profound understanding and sincere practice, so as to truly learn with firm belief, learn with absolute loyalty and learn with a sense of mission and responsibility.
We must carry out the decisions and arrangements of the 20th CPC National Congress with a spirit of arduous struggle, solidly promote the modernization of China in our own way, work hard, roll up our sleeves, act as the "construction supervisor", and turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
To strengthen the ability to drive high-quality development, serve the people, and prevent and resolve risks, we should vigorously develop the spirit of investigation and research, and resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Xi Jinping, Li Keqiang, Li Shiwei, Chen Wenquing, Liu Jinkun, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, and Chen Si presided over the ceremony.
The last communist premier of East Germany dies today
The successor of the East German Communist Party reported in a statement that “Last night, Hans Modrow left us at the age of 95.
As a result, our party has lost an important leader.
“
On November 13, 1989, four days after the opening of the Berlin Wall, which separated East Berlin and West Berlin for 28 years, Modrow said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic country.
At the time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to step down as protesters across East Germany demanded democracy and freedom.
After the Soviet Union came to power, Mikhail Gorbachev called for changes in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe as well.
In March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election in the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election results led to him no longer serving as Prime Minister.
Despite Mordor's reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political changes and reunification that took place in October 1990.
He has also been criticized for trying to reform the secret police rather than abolish it.
In 1993, Modro was convicted of electoral fraud in the May 1989 municipal elections, but was not jailed.
It is said that these accusations are politically motivated.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued his parliamentary career in Germany and served as an MEP from 1999 to 2004.
Modro sees himself as a reformer and wants to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want the old East Germany to return, but said that the achievements of East Germany should be recognized.
Modrow was born in 1928 in the then German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland), and was trained as a mechanic.
During World War II, he served as a platoon leader in the youth fire brigade and, as the conflict drew to a close, became a member of the Nazi militia organization, the Volkssturm, which conscripted men aged 16 to 60 for the final struggle of the war.
When he was 17, Modrow was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he took part in anti-fascist courses and became a staunch communist.
In 1949, the year of the establishment of East Germany, he returned to his home country and found a job as a mechanic. He continued to study social sciences and economics and obtained a doctorate.
Modrow was a staff member of the Free German Youth movement, which almost all East German young people joined, and rose to become the chairman of the party in the Dresden region between 1973 and 1989 through the ruling Socialist Unity Party (SED).
He also served in the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest state office.
Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung and his wife have successfully completed their official visits to Singapore and Brunei, achieving comprehensive, practical and specific outcomes, VNA reported.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng participated in more than 30 different activities.
The results achieved have provided new impetus for the further development of the new strategic partnership between the two countries and the Vietnamese Comprehensive Partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During the visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reiterate the foreign policy line of the Party and the State of Vietnam, namely independence, diversity, and variability, and the willingness to be a good friend and reliable partner of all countries, as well as a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in each country’s interest to promote the welfare of its people and contribute to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
At the meetings and talks, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh agreed with the leaders of Singapore and Brunei to continuously strengthen political trust with Vietnam through the exchange of high-level delegations, effective operation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements, etc.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore sign a memorandum of understanding on green and digital economic partnership.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During meetings with business leaders, seminars or attendance at economic forums, PM Fan Minh Diem stressed that Vietnam welcomes and facilitates the expansion of investment in the fields of digital transformation, green energy, high technology, innovative innovation and other areas by Singaporean and Brunei enterprises.
This visit will not only help deepen the cooperation between Vietnam, Singapore and Brunei in various traditional fields such as politics, foreign affairs, economy, security, national defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, and people-to-people exchanges, but also create a cooperation framework for the two countries in new potential fields such as digital economy, green economy, energy transformation, innovation and creativity, smart city, and sustainable development.
King Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Premier Wen Jiabao are preparing to enter a bilateral meeting.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During the visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and wishes of the Vietnamese community living in the localities.
During the meeting between the leaders of the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh suggested that the two countries' authorities should pay more attention to and ensure fair treatment for local Vietnamese communities, create favorable conditions for contributing to local society and cultivating the relationship between the two countries.
The proposal was approved and supported by the leaders of both countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Mingyi also shared with the leaders of the two countries the desire for a united, peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN community; agreed to maintain united cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance the central role of ASEAN in the complex and changing context of regional and international situations.
Based on the important results achieved, Prime Minister Fan Minh Diệm's official visits to Singapore and Brunei will contribute positively to the effective implementation of the 13th CPC General Assembly's priority foreign policy to strengthen relations with ASEAN neighbours, the effective implementation of the CPC Central Political Bureau's Conclusion No. 12 on Vietnam's work in the new situation ((12-KL/TW) and the development of the National Solidarity Force.
(Finish)
NEWS GOV-MO: Alert: Police Department urges citizens to be wary of fake text messages from telecom companies
Recently, the Police Bureau received multiple reports of telecommunications fraud cases where criminals impersonated local telecom companies and sent fraudulent SMSs containing links to fake websites, promising rewards for exchanging points that were about to expire.
The victim followed the instructions to enter the credit card information and verification code, and then received a notification from the financial institution that there were unidentified records of consumption on the credit card. The victim suspected that the credit card information had been stolen from the above website.
After investigation, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunications company did not send the above short message.
The police urge the public to be vigilant when receiving similar text messages and not to click on the links in the text messages or provide any personal information. If you are asked to provide credit card information, account transaction passwords or transaction verification codes, you should be doubly cautious to prevent credit card theft.
Scam alert:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity information and improve personal prevention awareness.
Do not casually log onto unknown websites and register your personal and credit card information there to prevent identity theft;
3. Beware of fake websites and phishing websites, and always pay attention to whether the website address is completely consistent with the official website.
4. Install antivirus software on your mobile phone, mobile device or computer and update it regularly.
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: the process of reception is stalled - China News
EU summit is in a dilemma over the refugee policy, and EU officials said that every step of the reception process has bottlenecks
According to a report by Agence France-Presse on February 10, at the latest EU summit on that day, the President of the European Commission, von der Leyen, said that the leaders of the European Union agreed to introduce stricter policies on illegal immigrants, so that it would be easier to expel illegal immigrants.
The EU's move is reportedly in response to growing concerns about illegal immigration in Europe, where the EU's core problem is that few illegal immigrants are ultimately repatriated.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to immediately mobilize large amounts of EU funds to strengthen the external borders through infrastructure and surveillance.
However, the EU is in constant dispute with its member states over issues such as the payment of the fence fee.
Frauenfeld repeatedly stated that EU funds would not cover related costs.
But some member state diplomats said that if the EU could share the cost of installing cameras, watchtowers and other infrastructure along its external borders, it would free up national budgets and speed up the construction process.
The European Union’s Euractiv website reports that EU officials acknowledge that there are bottlenecks at every stage of the refugee reception process and that the limited capacity to receive refugees and member states’ overwhelmed immigration authorities cannot prevent refugees from submitting “numerous” asylum applications in all EU countries, putting the EU’s refugee reception system on an almost permanent crisis footing.
The European Commission estimates that in 2017, EU Schengen countries received over 920,000 asylum applications, up nearly half from the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded over 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle" that EU countries could deport illegal immigrants back to their home countries based on a court decision of another member country.
In addition, the report said EU leaders also agreed to increase the use of the term "security state", which would pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
The Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Xia Lijiang, visited China to convey the message of Song Tao: welcome the Green Party to visit China under the consensus of 92.
The Vice Chairman of the Chinese Nationalist Party in Taiwan, Shih Lien-jang, met with the Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Song Tao, and the member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, Wang Meng.
Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor of the Nationalist Party’s official institution, the Guoguang Foundation, was interviewed by the Central News Agency of Taiwan yesterday evening. He actively praised Song Taizheng for his words to Xia Litian, saying that China welcomes Green Party people to visit the mainland as long as they acknowledge the “92 Consensus” and are against Taiwan independence.
The Nationalist Party considered it a new thing.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling People's Democratic Party of Taiwan has repeatedly made clear that it does not accept the 1992 Consensus.
According to Central News Agency today, the delegation led by the Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Shali Lian, visited the mainland. During their stay in Beijing, they met with the member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee Wang Meng, the new Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, Song Tao, and the Secretary of the Beijing Municipal Committee, Yin Li.
Xia Litian and Song Tao talked about the political basis of the national government and the anti-Taiwan independence, and Zhao Chunshan, senior advisor of the National Party’s National Government Fund, said in the meeting that the National Party’s “nine-two consensus” is the original “nine-two consensus”.
Zhao Chunshan notes that this is different from his previous experiences at meetings.
Recently, I had a video conference with scholars from the mainland, and in this conference, I did not hear any words about the suppression of Taiwan and the “anti-secession law”. Instead, the focus was on the resumption of exchanges and dialogue.
Liu Chunhan pointed out that the two sides are at risk of a bloody war and that mainland China hopes to communicate its intention to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the CPC and the DPP, the other party still wants to do a good job for the people of Taiwan, and the representative does not want to ruin the relationship between the two sides.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Hongwen also personally gave instructions to Song Tao to tell "you must implement the requests made by them (Taiwanese farmers and fishermen)" and if it is not possible to solve it comprehensively, it should be handled on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the KMT visitor to the mainland directly mentioned the daily disruption of the Taiwanese border by Chinese military aircraft, the problem of farming and fishing in a few Taiwanese counties, or whether the interview with a reporter from the Central News Agency asked such questions.
What was "the object" that crashed in the airspace above阿拉斯加?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
The US military again deployed the most advanced US stealth fighter F-22 on Friday afternoon, shooting down an unidentified object flying over Alaska, USA.
The crash site is 10 miles off the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time the US has shot down an airborne object in less than a week.
A Chinese spy balloon was shot down over the US coast of South Carolina on Saturday, days after it was floating over US airspace.
The Pentagon said the second object, which first entered U.S. airspace on Thursday night, was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), was about the size of a small car and much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon that was shot down earlier.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no evidence to suggest that this object can be controlled.
John Coby, White House National Security Council strategic communications coordinator, said Friday that while the exact nature of the object flying high in the sky is not clear, it poses a legitimate threat to the safety of civil aviation aircraft.
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe said, "We call it an 'object' because it's the best description we can give it at this point."
President Biden listened to the Pentagon's advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was very cautious in making the decision, Corby added.
The official description of the object in the United States can be roughly summarized as: It was the size of a small car, without a handlebar, no suspension, and was flying at an altitude of about 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It could be from China, like the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that was hovering over Latin America, both of which are performing a mission in different locations.
And some have linked this “object” in Alaska to UFOs.
The US Newsweek report quoted former US Congressman Peter Meijer as tweeting on Friday that he really hoped the UFO was a spy balloon and not a legitimate UFO.
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Mejia tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
According to the news magazine, it is not just Mayer who is suspicious of the object being a UFO.
Republican Representative Tim Burchett of Tennessee criticized the government's cover-up last month, demanding that the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) publish a report on the UFO sighting.
Xi Jinping sent a letter to encourage the members of the Chinese medical team in Africa. They should show love and care to the local people and tell the Chinese story with their deeds. - Rolling News - Hunan Daily Network - Huasheng Online
Xi Jinping sent a letter of encouragement to the Chinese medical team in Africa, urging them to use their medical skills to help the local people and to tell the Chinese story with their deeds.
February 11, 2023 at 1:09 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large medium small】
Xinhua Beijing, Feb. 10 (Xinhua) -- General Secretary, President and Chairman of the Central Military Commission of the Communist Party of China (CPC), Xi Jinping, on February 9 replied to the Chinese medical team members of the 19th aid mission to the Central African Republic, sending greetings and expressing his best wishes to them and to the vast medical team.
In response, Xi Jinping said that you in Central Africa, who overcome the difficulties of working life and serve the local people with all your heart, are both angels in white who save the dead and the wounded and friendly messengers of good wishes.
This year marks the 60th anniversary of China’s dispatching medical teams abroad; I extend sincere greetings to all comrades who have and continue to serve in international medical missions.
Xi Jinping pointed out that China’s people love peace and cherish life, which is vividly illustrated in medical aid missions abroad.
I hope that you will not forget your original intention and remember your mission, and vigorously carry forward the spirit of the Chinese medical team of not being afraid of hardship, being willing to make sacrifices, saving lives and treating injuries, and showing boundless love. Use your kindness and medical skills to benefit the local people, tell the Chinese story with practical actions, and make greater contributions to promoting the construction of a community with a shared future for mankind.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria.
Over six decades, China has dispatched over 300,000 medical personnel to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, America, Europe, and Oceania, treating more than 290 million patients, winning widespread acclaim from the international community.
Currently, the medical teams are working in 115 medical facilities in 56 countries around the world, with almost half of them in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of China’s medical teams dispatched to Central Africa wrote letters to President Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts in implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and providing medical services for local residents, as well as expressing their determination to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.
Iranian revolution anniversary: Hacker supporting protests hijacks presidential speech
An official rally was held on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Islamic Revolution in Iran, but an anti-government hacker briefly interrupted a televised speech by President Ibrahim Raisi.
The president’s televised address was interrupted for about a minute on the Internet, and a group of Iranian hackers known as “Edalat Ali (Ali Justice)” appeared on screen.
There was also a voice shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic."
Reuters reports that Iran is commemorating its revolution anniversary and hackers have disrupted national TV broadcasts.
Iranian officials mark 44th anniversary of Islamic Revolution; Shiraz’s hardliners face biggest challenge yet from young protesters demanding their ouster but still urges “deceived youth” to repent so they can be pardoned by Iran’s supreme leader.
The wave of nationwide protests continues in Iran after the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in September in the custody of the country's moral police.
The deadly crackdown on protests by Iranian security forces is one of the biggest challenges facing the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution that toppled the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty to commemorate the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities released imprisoned dissidents Fahad Mesami and Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha on Friday for their hunger strike protests.
Earlier, the Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty decree, which includes some prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to human rights organization HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters had been killed, including 71 minors.
The report said that 70 other government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and state media have been calling for a vote at Saturday's rally to show opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On the eve of the anniversary of the Iranian revolution on Friday night, state media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, with people chanting "Allahu Akbar!"
“God is the greatest!”
However, many people at the rally were also heard shouting "Death to the dictator!"
and the 'death of the Islamic Republic' in videos posted on social media.
Saturday, the government TV broadcast live footage of official gatherings across all states.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestic anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lacey's speeches are often interrupted by the slogan "Fire to America", a signature slogan at state rallies.
The crowd also shouted “Death to Israel”.
Reuters said that Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, which is a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on national security charges.
They later placed her under house arrest, but she returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denied these allegations.
A week before Mesami was released, supporters warned that he was in danger of death as a result of the hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting against the compulsory wearing of headscarves.
The French Foreign Ministry responded to Adelkhah's release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, including the possibility of her being allowed to return to France if she wishes.
