Currently, there is no official feedback channel for Amazon, so you can only give feedback in the product reviews.
1. On March 29, I purchased the book for 31 yuan through pre-order, and it showed that it would be pushed to my device on March 31. At this time, I could not preview the book on Amazon's official website (because it had not been published yet);
The book sent to the device on March 31 was blank, with only "Please look forward to it", and the electronic version of the book on Amazon was reduced to 18 yuan.
I have repeatedly tried to delete the blank book downloaded from the device and synchronize it again, but I can not get the electronic version of "the essence of business" with actual content, but I can preview the book on the official website of Amazon.
I have some thoughts to share at this point.
1. The price issue is not really the most important thing; what’s more crucial is how to turn Kindle’s blank books into ones with actual content rather than always downloading “coming soon.”
2. I won't buy the pre-ordered book anymore, because if I jump the queue, it will be very complicated to download a book with empty content.
3. I hope Amazon provides a normal channel to report such issues; when there is any doubt about downloading or using e-books, one can have an outlet to feedback (e.g., through tickets or online customer service). This can be similar to how Microsoft’s official store handles it.
Lonely little lion
When I got the book, I thought it would be as simple as The Lost Piece of Paper, but turns out there's still a lot of text!
After reading it three times, I finally read this book to the children, a little lion that can shoot guns and one that loves juice-flavored lollipops.
When I saw the scene of the lion eating the hunter, I felt a little uncomfortable, and modern city people can’t accept such an arrangement of being eaten by animals.
In the end, this little lion who succeeded in human society has lost himself; he is no longer entirely a lion nor an entirely human being.
Finally, only the silhouette of the little lion is left, and I don't know where he went.
Perhaps years later, the image of the little lion will remain in the minds of the child who has grown up and will be remembered at an unforeseen moment, perhaps touching or inspiring her.
